# Architecture Decision Records

Format precedent: `docs/organization/adr/0001-baseline-architecture.md`. Sections: Status,
Date, Deciders, Context, Decision, Alternatives Considered, Consequences, Revisit Trigger.

## Current ADR index (check before assuming a number is free)

- **0001** — baseline stack (React/Vite web, Expo mobile, Node/TS backend, MongoDB).
- **0002** — polyglot persistence: Supabase for identity, MongoDB for domain data.
- **0003** — backend hosting platform (Render).
- **0006** — privileged-access audit correlation (join key across the two audit trails).
  Status: **Ratified** by `cto` 2026-08-11 (§16), with five rulings R-1…R-5 and four
  conditions at §16.5. **§17 is a later same-day `cto` append** correcting one factual error
  inside §16 and adding FU-A13/FU-A14 — read §16 *and* §17 together; §16 was deliberately not
  edited, so reading it alone will leave you believing an index exists that doesn't.
- **0008** — MongoDB schema provisioning mechanism. Status: **Ratified** by `cto` 2026-08-24,
  with three conditions. **Condition 1 ("applied, never verified" catalog-provisioning
  language) stays open** until `devops-engineer` confirms the catalog-verification check
  actually runs in the deploy path (`docs/organization/sprint-plan-release-gate-a.md` item
  1.4/2.8) — don't treat ratification alone as closing that condition.
- **0009** — self-asserted location ingestion is a new, distinct trust boundary from ADR-0006's
  third trail (governs Feature 008 self-device GPS tracking; does not reopen or amend ADR-0006).
  Status: **Ratified** by `cto` 2026-08-24 (§17), conditionally — the ADR-level precedent and
  SDL-1…SDL-12 are binding. **§15 (`security-engineer` concurrence) and §16
  (`compliance-specialist` concurrence) remain reserved and unfiled** — conditions on the
  ratification, not discharged by it. **§18 is a 2026-08-25 append correcting §14/§17.4's false
  claim that no ingestion endpoint existed** — read §18 before citing either section; the
  endpoint had already shipped past this ADR's explicit prohibition (INC-001). **§9 of INC-001
  records `cybersecurity-architect` withholding Release Gate A criterion-6 sign-off (2026-08-28)
  pending remediation** — read `docs/organization/incidents/INC-001-location-ingestion.md`
  before assuming this area is clear to build on. Read
  `docs/features/008-self-device-gps-tracking/` and INC-001 before touching anything this ADR
  governs.

**0004 and 0005 are reserved by name** in existing documents (FU-03 deletion-vs-anonymization
ADR; Feature 003's session-token contract ADR, referenced as M-09) but not yet written —
don't reuse either number for an unrelated decision. **0007** is reserved for FU-08's
third-persistence-surface ADR (ADR-0006 ruling R-4). **0010 is reserved for the payment gateway
vendor decision** (per `docs/organization/sprint-plan-release-gate-a.md` item 4.1/4.2 —
scorecard/decision due Sprint 4, ratification to follow) — not yet written as of this file's
last sync. **The next genuinely free number is 0011** — re-verify against
`docs/organization/adr/` before relying on this line; it has drifted before.

## Before writing a new ADR

Check whether the decision is actually ADR-level: a reversible vendor pick behind a clean
interface (e.g. the SMTP vendor choice) was explicitly judged *not* to need one — see
`docs/features/001-authentication/smtp-vendor-selection.md` §9 for that reasoning as the
precedent for "is this ADR-worthy" judgment calls. A decision that interprets or extends an
already-ratified ADR, or that sets a rule future decisions will inherit by reference, does
need one — ADR-0006 is the precedent for that side of the line.
